      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5bdba93899e4d70e980e91ee",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Shift-F2 is \"Fist\". We don't generally recommend putting overrides that trigger objects/particles/etc on fist, as it is an \"Analog\" gesture (it blends from 0 to 100 based on your trigger position). As you might expect, you can't really have an object partially enabled, or particles partially on.\n\nThis is a known issue, but with no immediate plans for a fix. Our current recommendation for a workaround is to avoid putting gestures on the \"Fist\" override unless it only affects finger position. Adding other animated qualities to the \"Fist\" override may result in a lot of strange behavior.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-11-02T01:32:40.412Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When you first enter a world, the F2 emote is on by default, instead of F1, but only for others and not yourself. It is only fixed by pressing a different emote, and then pressing F1. This can cause issues like playing music that only others can hear, causing objects that are only supposed to appear when pressing F2 to appear by default, and changes your face to an unintended emote. This happens to both VR users and Desktop Users.",
